slock - simple screen locker
============================

Upstream usage reference, with build requirements adapted for this fork.
For this desktop’s installation, startup, and rebuild workflow, see
[the local setup guide](README.md). The standalone instructions below
do not replace the repository installer or its session launcher.
simple screen locker utility for X.


Requirements
------------
This build requires a C compiler, Make, and development headers and libraries for Xlib, Xext, Xrandr, and libcrypt.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (slock is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install slock
(if necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running slock
-------------
Simply invoke the 'slock' command. To get out of it, enter your password.

[Documentation index](../../../README.md#documentation)
